    "text": "A thin convex lens <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> (refractive index <math><mo>=</mo><mn>1.5</mn></math> ) is placed on a plane mirror <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>. When a pin is placed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, such that <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> its real inverted image is formed at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> itself, as shown in figure. When liquid of refractive index <math><msub><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></math> is put between the lens and the mirror, the pin has to be moved to <math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>'</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> such that <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">'</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn><mtext> </mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> to get its inverted real image at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi>'</mi></math> itself. The value of <math><msub><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></math> will be<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/WhatsApp_Image_2020-07-04_at_1.13.24_PM.jpeg\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 167px;\" />",
